     while (candies <= k) {
       candies += sum;
       sum++;
       n--;
     }
     // Reduce candies to less than k
     const candiesToSubtract = candies - k;
     n -= candiesToSubtract;
     consumed += candiesToSubtract;
     candies -= candiesToSubtract;
   }

 This is a bit tricky: the inner loop runs while candies <= k, and each iteration increases candies and sum, and decreases n.
 Then after the inner loop, candies > k. Then we subtract (candies - k) from candies, and also subtract that amount from n, and add to consumed.

 We'll keep the same logic.

